<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">SES S.A.</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1985</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Société Européenne des Satellites</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">SES is a satellite telecommunications company founded in Luxembourg in 1985 as the Société Européenne des Satellites, with the Luxembourg state as a major shareholder. Its first Astra satellite, launched in 1988, pioneered direct-to-home satellite television across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and the company grew into one of the world's largest satellite operators. Its headquarters remain at Betzdorf in Luxembourg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ses-s-a.jpg" alt="SES S.A." width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GilPe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betzdorf,_SES_(110).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
